f you don't like Python  it's a fish if you're really attached to  MATLAB  it's named after bird so for this this  is what virtus looks like and it's an  actual art package that's being used for  your color maps and this is a really  good color map because it's it can print  in grayscale you can its colorblind  friendly and you know Noam Ross who is  one of our speakers you know put this  together for the art community and one  thing I want to talk about is like hey  there's color maps start thinking about  you know specific color maps  for yourself for specific variables so  when you're working as a group you don't  have to you know think too much about  what you're looking at and there was a  great talk from the Python community as  well about how an oceanographer has  specific color maps that they put  together and if you really can't be  bothered you know there's the color  Brewer which I use to just help you pick  really good color maps so you can call  it you can check off like if it's  colorblind save or print friendly and  you can get like a nice color map out of  it for yourself as well and then other  things you know make cookbooks as needed  make your own flight rules there's a  really good flight rule repository about  like how you can use git without you  know just starting over and we cloning  things and then so why am I telling all  of this well from Greg Wilson our planet  needs our help and we need good science  to fix it so thanks everyone again thank  you  you
 

